      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-22T10:26:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you should not need to lock anything as you are setting this under the device lock, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "e43ba023452692e322cf38f022b467757f12997c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ca9cf71_7f5e8ec8",
        "filename": "drivers/of/platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1446383
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-22T15:50:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are no locks grabbed anywhere in the call path as far as I can see because this is a new device being created. I think we need a lock here so that get_device()\u0027s view (called from  of_find_device_by_node()) doesn\u0027t change while it\u0027s trying to get the device. It\u0027s arguable that I don\u0027t need a lock here and only need a lock when I set it to NULL, but that seem weird to grab it only sometimes.",
      "parentUuid": "9ba245ef_d75fdee2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "e43ba023452692e322cf38f022b467757f12997c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8977e55_774882ee",
        "filename": "drivers/of/platform.c",
